- They had to be bigger.
- They were cruel.

1268
00:43:23,099 --> 00:43:24,969
(They pulled off an incredible miracle,)

1269
00:43:24,969 --> 00:43:26,109
I'm sorry.

1270
00:43:26,109 --> 00:43:27,539
(but in the end, they had to apologize.)

1271
00:43:28,039 --> 00:43:29,079
No.

1272
00:43:29,079 --> 00:43:30,679
(All presents are taken away.)

1273
00:43:30,679 --> 00:43:32,079
Gosh. For goodness' sake.

1274
00:43:32,079 --> 00:43:34,149
Gosh. I can't believe it didn't work.

1275
00:43:34,749 --> 00:43:36,149
(Staring)

1276
00:43:36,149 --> 00:43:37,949
This is too hard.

1277
00:43:39,549 --> 00:43:40,989
Korea is too good at manufacturing this stuff.

1278
00:43:41,489 --> 00:43:44,459
This can is so sturdy.

1279
00:43:46,329 --> 00:43:47,799
Gosh. We failed again.

1280
00:43:47,799 --> 00:43:49,159
(The "Made in Korea" brothers can't keep their heads up.)

1281
00:43:49,159 --> 00:43:50,299
It's all right.

1282
00:43:50,399 --> 00:43:51,699
- It's okay. Really.
- It's okay.

1283
00:43:51,699 --> 00:43:53,439
- We're sorry.
- It's all right.

1284
00:43:53,439 --> 00:43:55,099
- It's okay.
- You should get them first.

1285
00:43:55,269 --> 00:43:56,769
Okay. It's all right.

1286
00:43:56,909 --> 00:43:58,669
- What a shame.
- It suits me well.

1287
00:43:59,009 --> 00:44:00,079
Thank you.

1288
00:44:00,079 --> 00:44:01,509
(Loving it)

1289
00:44:01,509 --> 00:44:02,609
Okay.

1290
00:44:03,039 --> 00:44:05,479
(Ashamed)

1291
00:44:05,479 --> 00:44:06,549
I'm so mad.

1292
00:44:07,379 --> 00:44:08,479
We apologize.

1293
00:44:08,479 --> 00:44:09,719
- It's all right.
- Thank you.

1294
00:44:09,719 --> 00:44:10,889
We'll get going.

1295
00:44:11,049 --> 00:44:12,119
Thank you.

1296
00:44:12,719 --> 00:44:15,389
Gosh. Why didn't it work?

1297
00:44:15,959 --> 00:44:18,759
I've rarely felt this sorry.

1298
00:44:18,759 --> 00:44:19,929
I feel so bad.

1299
00:44:19,929 --> 00:44:21,199
- It's a bad feeling.
- Yes.

1300
00:44:21,899 --> 00:44:23,129
Gosh. It was close.

1301
00:44:23,359 --> 00:44:24,669
(Anyway, it's time for lunch.)

1302
00:44:24,669 --> 00:44:26,399
Anyang Big Star?

1303
00:44:26,769 --> 00:44:28,169
That must be it.

1304
00:44:28,169 --> 00:44:29,769
- The cab that's making a left turn.
- You're right.

1305
00:44:30,509 --> 00:44:31,709
Hello.

1306
00:44:31,709 --> 00:44:32,869
Hello.

1307
00:44:33,409 --> 00:44:34,509
Gosh.

1308
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:36,809
It'll only take 7 to 8 minutes.

1309
00:44:37,349 --> 00:44:40,249
(The mood is much gloomier than before.)

1310
00:44:41,019 --> 00:44:42,079
What a shame.

1311
00:44:42,079 --> 00:44:44,289
- It was really close.
- It was.

1312
00:44:44,689 --> 00:44:48,619
(He can't shake off the disappointment easily.)

1313
00:44:49,019 --> 00:44:51,659
- Do you feel like this every week?
- That's right.

1314
00:44:52,889 --> 00:44:55,099
Even if you succeeded during practice,

1315
00:44:55,529 --> 00:44:56,829
when the game begins,

1316
00:44:56,829 --> 00:44:59,369
and when the countdown begins, you can't do it.

1317
00:44:59,529 --> 00:45:00,799
"Five, four, three..."

1318
00:45:01,369 --> 00:45:02,399
That was you, Hyun Bin.

1319
00:45:02,399 --> 00:45:03,709
The moment I heard "five..."

1320
00:45:04,309 --> 00:45:05,639
- Did it make you nervous?
- Yes, it did.

1321
00:45:05,639 --> 00:45:07,739
- It makes you hurry.
- Yes, I felt rushed.

1322
00:45:11,609 --> 00:45:13,249
Gosh. We had our chances.

1323
00:45:13,249 --> 00:45:15,419
We had a couple of crucial chances.

1324
00:45:15,779 --> 00:45:17,749
- That's right.
- But we couldn't pull it off.

1325
00:45:18,489 --> 00:45:19,989
So, I keep thinking,

1326
00:45:20,419 --> 00:45:22,289
"Should we have used the big ball at first?"

1327
00:45:24,329 --> 00:45:26,229
Stop talking about the big ball.

1328
00:45:27,759 --> 00:45:29,699
No, I'm not saying it was Do Hwan's fault.

1329
00:45:30,199 --> 00:45:31,769
I wondered if we should've used the big ball at first.

1330
00:45:32,399 --> 00:45:33,839
- That's all, Do Hwan.
- What? Okay.

1331
00:45:33,839 --> 00:45:35,369
- I got it.
- Should we have used it at first?

1332
00:45:35,369 --> 00:45:38,139
If we used it, we might have pulled it off.

1333
00:45:38,369 --> 00:45:39,569
What a shame.

1334
00:45:40,179 --> 00:45:41,439
I'm getting more determined.

1335
00:45:42,479 --> 00:45:43,609
Gosh.

1336
00:45:44,979 --> 00:45:46,749
I should check what's around the place.

1337
00:45:48,849 --> 00:45:51,549
- Yes, that's right.
- Since we have a mouth...

1338
00:45:52,189 --> 00:45:53,919
Since we have a mouth, we have to eat something.

1339
00:45:53,919 --> 00:45:54,989
We should eat.

1340
00:45:55,359 --> 00:45:56,789
It's your birthday today, Jae Seok.

1341
00:45:56,789 --> 00:45:58,789
- Don't mind me.
- Wouldn't it be nice and cool?

1342
00:45:58,789 --> 00:46:00,229
Should we get some seaweed soup?

1343
00:46:00,359 --> 00:46:02,129
- Seaweed soup!
- That's good.

1344
00:46:03,099 --> 00:46:04,869
- You had it in the morning, right?
- Yes, I did.

1345
00:46:05,529 --> 00:46:07,739
Come on, Yeon Seok. Seriously.

1346
00:46:08,169 --> 00:46:09,469
You already had it in the morning.

1347
00:46:10,369 --> 00:46:12,309
Look how thoughtful Hyun Bin is.

1348
00:46:14,609 --> 00:46:15,939
Let's have what you want to have.

1349
00:46:15,939 --> 00:46:17,809
- No, I have nothing in mind.
- Yes.

1350
00:46:18,509 --> 00:46:20,449
I don't crave anything. What do you want, Do Hwan?

1351
00:46:20,449 --> 00:46:21,679
- You're back in your hometown.
- What about bossam and makguksu?

1352
00:46:21,679 --> 00:46:22,819
Sounds good, Yeon Seok.

1353
00:46:23,079 --> 00:46:24,219
Where is it?

1354
00:46:24,349 --> 00:46:26,749
There's a bossam place in this alleyway.

1355
00:46:26,749 --> 00:46:28,459
- They have makguksu too.
- Bossam.

1356
00:46:29,089 --> 00:46:30,329
They've just opened.

1357
00:46:31,159 --> 00:46:32,229
- Where?
- For lunch?

1358
00:46:32,229 --> 00:46:34,229
For lunch. It opens at 11:20am.

1359
00:46:34,229 --> 00:46:36,159
- They've just opened.
- That's perfect.

1360
00:46:36,899 --> 00:46:38,829
Gosh. Do you really go to a place without pre-arranging it?

1361
00:46:38,829 --> 00:46:40,129
- Yes.
- Amazing. I've never done that.

1362
00:46:40,769 --> 00:46:42,569
- They've just opened.
- We're right on time.

1363
00:46:42,569 --> 00:46:43,769
(They arrive in time for opening.)

1364
00:46:43,769 --> 00:46:44,869
It's nice and cool.

1365
00:46:45,569 --> 00:46:47,539
The aftermath of the last game lingers.

1366
00:46:48,739 --> 00:46:49,839
Right?

1367
00:46:49,839 --> 00:46:51,249
(Setting the utensils as soon as he sits down)

1368
00:46:51,249 --> 00:46:52,609
It was so...

1369
00:46:52,779 --> 00:46:54,479
- What is this?
- I mean, it went too fast.

1370
00:46:54,479 --> 00:46:56,989
(The youngest one is quick and efficient.)

1371
00:46:58,319 --> 00:46:59,949
- Okay. Let's do better.
- Yes.

1372
00:47:00,219 --> 00:47:01,359
I'll do my best.

1373
00:47:01,859 --> 00:47:03,559
Gosh. It stays with you for a long time.

1374
00:47:03,889 --> 00:47:06,259
- I still see it.
- You can still see it.

1375
00:47:06,729 --> 00:47:09,429
- You can still see the last can.
- It's a bit...

1376
00:47:09,659 --> 00:47:10,829
It wasn't that bad.

1377
00:47:11,499 --> 00:47:13,229
Hyun Bin was exhilarated before.

1378
00:47:14,199 --> 00:47:16,469
I was thrilled up until Round Two.

1379
00:47:17,939 --> 00:47:19,169
He was so excited.

1380
00:47:19,169 --> 00:47:21,139
(Feeling disappointed again)

1381
00:47:21,139 --> 00:47:23,609
Have you watched us play games at home?

1382
00:47:23,609 --> 00:47:24,749
- Of course.
- I see.

1383
00:47:24,909 --> 00:47:26,049
When you were watching,

1384
00:47:26,209 --> 00:47:28,819
were there any games you thought you'd succeed?

1385
00:47:29,379 --> 00:47:31,319
Actually,

1386
00:47:31,989 --> 00:47:34,219
if you had asked me this question before the last game,

1387
00:47:34,219 --> 00:47:35,689
I would've answered it.

1388
00:47:36,519 --> 00:47:38,759
Now, I can't say anything.

1389
00:47:38,759 --> 00:47:40,859
When this is aired on TV,

1390
00:47:41,629 --> 00:47:44,869
Ye Jin will probably watch it with you.

1391
00:47:46,969 --> 00:47:49,069
(I really have to succeed in the next mission.)

1392
00:47:49,069 --> 00:47:50,569
You should succeed before you leave.

1393
00:47:51,339 --> 00:47:52,409
That's right.

1394
00:47:52,539 --> 00:47:54,239
- Gosh, look at these.
- Gosh.

1395
00:47:54,939 --> 00:47:56,309
- They are fancy.
- Our useless mouths...

1396
00:47:56,479 --> 00:47:57,909
Our useless mouths will be eating.

1397
00:47:57,909 --> 00:47:58,949
(Garlic bossam and octopus combo)

1398
00:47:59,179 --> 00:48:00,649
It's well-cooked. It must be tasty.

1399
00:48:01,819 --> 00:48:03,919
You have to eat it with the octopus.

1400
00:48:04,389 --> 00:48:06,249
You make a combo out of it.

1401
00:48:06,649 --> 00:48:07,659
(Satisfied)

1402
00:48:09,289 --> 00:48:12,259
I've never had bossam with octopus.

1403
00:48:14,159 --> 00:48:15,499
That went really well.

1404
00:48:16,129 --> 00:48:17,729
He's like Jang Geum in "Jewel in the Palace."

1405
00:48:18,629 --> 00:48:19,769
(He's mixing makguksu.)

1406
00:48:19,769 --> 00:48:21,099
Please enjoy your meal comfortably.

1407
00:48:21,099 --> 00:48:22,999
Do Hwan's mixing the noodles with his hand right now.

1408
00:48:23,869 --> 00:48:25,509
He's like Jang Geum in "Jewel in the Palace."

1409
00:48:25,509 --> 00:48:26,769
He's good.

1410
00:48:27,609 --> 00:48:29,779
Where did you learn this?

1411
00:48:30,409 --> 00:48:33,379
(He places it neatly on a plate and serves it to the brothers.)

1412
00:48:33,379 --> 00:48:34,549
He's very skillful.

1413
00:48:35,319 --> 00:48:37,819
- Thank you.
- Were you the youngest somewhere?

1414
00:48:39,289 --> 00:48:41,189
He's caring for us intuitively.

1415
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:42,489
He's like a good younger brother.

1416
00:48:42,919 --> 00:48:45,159
- Have you worked part-time before?
- Yes. Many times.

1417
00:48:45,159 --> 00:48:46,729
- Really?
- For what kind of jobs?

1418
00:48:47,359 --> 00:48:51,469
I've worked at many bakeries.

1419
00:48:52,769 --> 00:48:54,439
I also worked as a server at fried chicken places.

1420
00:48:54,439 --> 00:48:56,169
- Things like that.
- Exactly. We can tell.

1421
00:48:56,339 --> 00:48:58,169
Also at a pho place.

1422
00:48:58,169 --> 00:49:00,109
- I've done many part-time jobs.
- You look professional.

1423
00:49:00,109 --> 00:49:01,209
- Yes.
- Right.

1424
00:49:01,509 --> 00:49:04,079
- He looked like a pro.
- Yes, he did.

1425
00:49:05,609 --> 00:49:08,949
(Slurping the makguksu Do Hwan mixed)

1426
00:49:09,379 --> 00:49:11,319
Please cheer up after eating it.

1427
00:49:11,319 --> 00:49:12,419
Okay.

1428
00:49:16,689 --> 00:49:17,859
I have a lot on my mind.

1429
00:49:19,359 --> 00:49:20,759
We won't fail anymore.

1430
00:49:21,229 --> 00:49:22,259
We'll nail it in one go.

1431
00:49:22,659 --> 00:49:24,369
Whatever it is, we'll nail it on the first try.

1432
00:49:24,869 --> 00:49:25,969
Hold on.

1433
00:49:25,969 --> 00:49:27,499
(No more failures.)

1434
00:49:27,839 --> 00:49:29,039
Gosh. It was good.

1435
00:49:30,169 --> 00:49:31,169
By the way,

1436
00:49:31,169 --> 00:49:33,339
- we should play a game now.
- A game.

1437
00:49:33,909 --> 00:49:35,509
- Do you have your own credit cards?
- Yes.

1438
00:49:35,509 --> 00:49:36,879
- Did you bring yours?
- Yes.

1439
00:49:37,179 --> 00:49:38,649
We're betting on lunch.

1440
00:49:39,509 --> 00:49:41,319
Whose idea was it to pay with a personal card?

1441
00:49:42,479 --> 00:49:43,549
It just happened that way.

1442
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:45,249
"It just happened."

1443
00:49:46,149 --> 00:49:48,389
- It just happened.
- The staff wouldn't pay.

1444
00:49:48,619 --> 00:49:50,189
Pouring water is fun too.

1445
00:49:50,559 --> 00:49:52,459
- Right.
- Without letting it overflow.

1446
00:49:53,229 --> 00:49:55,699
Let's use this one. It's clearer to see.

1447
00:49:55,699 --> 00:49:56,929
(Pouring water into the cup)

1448
00:49:56,929 --> 00:49:59,069
- Let's fill it up a bit.
- Do we use that bottle?

1449
00:49:59,999 --> 00:50:01,339
- Should we use this bottle?
- Let's pour with that bottle.

1450
00:50:01,339 --> 00:50:02,999
- Okay, let's do that.
- So it'll be clear and quick?

1451
00:50:02,999 --> 00:50:04,269
- Yes.
- I'll go first.

1452
00:50:04,269 --> 00:50:07,109
(Yeon Seok goes first.)

1453
00:50:08,639 --> 00:50:10,009
He's pushing it.

1454
00:50:10,009 --> 00:50:11,109
(A bold start)

1455
00:50:13,449 --> 00:50:15,249
(The 2nd player, Hyun Bin, is flustered.)

1456
00:50:15,249 --> 00:50:16,349
You went too far.

1457
00:50:16,479 --> 00:50:17,549
From the start?

1458
00:50:17,549 --> 00:50:19,119
(Hesitating)

1459
00:50:22,119 --> 00:50:23,619
Gosh. How do I do this?

1460
00:50:23,619 --> 00:50:24,629
(Standing up)

1461
00:50:26,189 --> 00:50:27,629
(Stopping after pouring a little)

1462
00:50:27,629 --> 00:50:28,759
Gosh. Look at that.

1463
00:50:28,759 --> 00:50:31,399
- Gosh. It's over.
- We have a long way to go.

1464
00:50:31,399 --> 00:50:33,099
- Do we have a long way to go?
- Yes, in my opinion.

1465
00:50:33,099 --> 00:50:35,339
- Really?
- It domes over the rim.

1466
00:50:36,699 --> 00:50:38,709
(Does it dome over it?)

1467
00:50:40,069 --> 00:50:41,979
- Gosh. That was crazy.
- Goodness.

1468
00:50:41,979 --> 00:50:44,179
- Now, it's a bit risky.
- Yes. Now, it's risky.

1469
00:50:44,179 --> 00:50:45,549
Is it even possible?

1470
00:50:45,949 --> 00:50:47,949
- They know it from experience.
- Exactly.

1471
00:50:49,379 --> 00:50:51,719
You can tell that it has risen quite a bit.

1472
00:50:51,719 --> 00:50:52,919
(The two with the experience have the upper hand.)

1473
00:50:57,189 --> 00:50:58,559
Just one drop.

1474
00:51:05,269 --> 00:51:07,269
I poured way more than I thought.

1475
00:51:08,099 --> 00:51:10,299
I poured more than I meant to.

1476
00:51:10,299 --> 00:51:11,939
Is this really possible?

1477
00:51:11,939 --> 00:51:13,209
I poured more than I wanted to.

1478
00:51:13,209 --> 00:51:15,809
Gosh. You actually did it.

1479
00:51:15,879 --> 00:51:17,579
- It's bulging over the rim, right?
- Is it Hyun Bin's... Hold on.

1480
00:51:17,679 --> 00:51:19,349
- It's bulging over, right?
- Yes.

1481
00:51:19,909 --> 00:51:21,619
It'll be over if the wind blows.

1482
00:51:22,219 --> 00:51:25,149
- Goodness.
- Gosh. It bulges over like that.

1483
00:51:25,819 --> 00:51:27,659
It'll be over within three tries.

1484
00:51:28,489 --> 00:51:30,189
- This is a 2-on-2 match.
- I'm in trouble.

1485
00:51:30,189 --> 00:51:31,259
I think so too.

1486
00:51:31,429 --> 00:51:33,589
- Jae Seok, let's team up.
- I'm off the hook for sure.

1487
00:51:33,929 --> 00:51:35,559
- I'll pass it to them.
- Okay. Go for it.

1488
00:51:43,739 --> 00:51:44,739
(A single drop)

1489
00:51:47,039 --> 00:51:48,039
(Touching)

1490
00:51:48,039 --> 00:51:50,009
(Amazed)

1491
00:51:50,009 --> 00:51:51,679
(Touched again)

1492
00:51:51,679 --> 00:51:52,849
He's so sly.

1493
00:51:52,849 --> 00:51:54,949
(It's a fine skill executed by the experienced one.)

1494
00:51:55,549 --> 00:51:57,189
Gosh. You really don't want to pay for lunch.

1495
00:51:59,289 --> 00:52:01,319
- Gosh.
- Gosh. It's like a pudding.

1496
00:52:01,319 --> 00:52:02,589
It's bulging high above the rim.

1497
00:52:02,589 --> 00:52:03,789
- It'll be over soon.
- Yes.

1498
00:52:03,789 --> 00:52:05,159
(It's Hyun Bin's turn again.)

1499
00:52:05,159 --> 00:52:06,389
It's so difficult.

1500
00:52:07,329 --> 00:52:08,929
- It's on them now.
- Yes.

1501
00:52:09,459 --> 00:52:10,499
Gosh.

1502
00:52:11,329 --> 00:52:14,169
- Hyun Bin.
- Is your neck really stiff?

1503
00:52:14,869 --> 00:52:17,669
Hyun Bin is suffering a lot.

1504
00:52:17,669 --> 00:52:19,009
(The variety show pros are relaxed.)

1505
00:52:20,609 --> 00:52:22,579
- You should go for it.
- What? Come on, Hyun Bin.

1506
00:52:25,479 --> 00:52:27,219
- Hyun Bin.
- Here we go.

1507
00:52:27,219 --> 00:52:28,219
Relax.

1508
00:52:34,819 --> 00:52:37,489
(Safe!)

1509
00:52:37,629 --> 00:52:39,629
- It didn't overflow.
- No, it didn't.

1510
00:52:39,859 --> 00:52:41,599
You can see the water rising above the rim, right?

1511
00:52:42,929 --> 00:52:44,829
He doesn't want to pay for lunch either.

1512
00:52:45,769 --> 00:52:47,239
The look on your face is so real.

1513
00:52:47,239 --> 00:52:48,339
(Hyun Bin who hates to pay for lunch does exist.)

1514
00:52:48,639 --> 00:52:50,069
